# Git author identity

Public git history must look like a human-only repo. Some players refuse mods with any AI association.

## When committing

- **Author and committer** are the existing git user (`AzraelGodKing`). Do not set `GIT_AUTHOR_*` / `GIT_COMMITTER_*` to Cursor, an agent, or any AI identity.
- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by:` trailers for Cursor, Cursor Agent, or any AI/tool.
- Do **not** mention AI, Cursor, Copilot, or agents in commit messages, changelogs, `About.xml`, Workshop notes, or player-facing text.
- Do **not** run `git config` to change `user.name` / `user.email` (leave the local identity as-is).
- If a hook or template injects an AI co-author line, strip it before the commit is created.

## Do not

```
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```

```
Made-with: Cursor
```
